Package: cantriple-socketcan
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Minton Performance <mitchminton@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3, python3-serial, iproute2, udev
Recommends: can-utils
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/mitchdetailed/CAN-Triple-Device-Manager
Description: CAN Triple 2.0 as a SocketCAN adapter
 The CAN Triple 2.0 can present itself to a PC as a gs_usb CAN adapter, the
 protocol of the Linux kernel's own gs_usb driver, so its three buses become
 SocketCAN interfaces with no driver to build: candump, cansend, python-can,
 SavvyCAN and every other SocketCAN program use them as they are.
 .
 This package binds gs_usb to the unit, names the interfaces after it and the
 bus (ct<unit>-can1 to -can3), optionally brings them up at set bit rates,
 and provides ctriple, which switches the unit between SocketCAN mode and the
 Device Manager's serial port, keeps the mode across power-ups, and brings the
 interfaces up and down.
 .
 Needs CAN Triple 2.0 firmware 2.0.7 or later (2.0.10 to keep the mode).
